---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Polynomials | CBSE Class 10 Maths | ${provider.name}`}
  description="CBSE Class 10 Maths Chapter 2 notes on Polynomials. Geometrical meaning of zeroes, quadratic parabola graphs, relationship between zeroes and coefficients, symmetric expressions, and an interactive 20-question board exam quiz."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> / Polynomials
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Mathematics · Chapter 2</span>
      <h1>Polynomials</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Understand zeroes of polynomials geometrically, master the relationship between zeroes and coefficients (sum &amp; product of roots), and ace board exam quadratic and cubic polynomial problems.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts &amp; Formulas</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>📈 Geometrical Meaning of Zeroes</h3>
          <p class="formula">Number of zeroes = Intersections with X-axis</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>A real number <em>k</em> is a zero of polynomial <em>p(x)</em> if <code>p(k) = 0</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Geometric interpretation:</strong> The zeroes of <em>y = p(x)</em> are the x-coordinates of the points where the graph intersects or touches the <strong>x-axis</strong>.</li>
            <li>A linear polynomial <em>ax + b</em> has at most <strong>1 real zero</strong> (straight line).</li>
            <li>A quadratic polynomial <em>ax² + bx + c</em> has at most <strong>2 real zeroes</strong> (U-shaped parabola).</li>
            <li>A cubic polynomial has at most <strong>3 real zeroes</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📐 Quadratic Polynomial Zeroes &amp; Coefficients</h3>
          <p class="formula">p(x) = ax² + bx + c, (a ≠ 0)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Let <em>α</em> and <em>β</em> be the zeroes of <em>p(x) = ax² + bx + c</em>:</li>
            <li><strong>Sum of zeroes:</strong> <code>α + β = -b / a = -(coefficient of x) / (coefficient of x²)</code></li>
            <li><strong>Product of zeroes:</strong> <code>α · β = c / a = (constant term) / (coefficient of x²)</code></li>
            <li><strong>Forming a polynomial:</strong> If sum <em>S</em> and product <em>P</em> are given, the quadratic polynomial is:
              <br/><code>k [x² - (α + β)x + αβ] = k [x² - Sx + P]</code> (where k is a non-zero constant).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔄 Important Algebraic Identites for Zeroes</h3>
          <p class="formula">Expressing in terms of (α + β) and (αβ)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><code>α² + β² = (α + β)² - 2αβ</code></li>
            <li><code>(α - β)² = (α + β)² - 4αβ &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; |α - β| = √((α + β)² - 4αβ)</code></li>
            <li><code>α³ + β³ = (α + β)³ - 3αβ(α + β) = (α + β)(α² - αβ + β²)</code></li>
            <li><code>1/α + 1/β = (α + β) / (αβ)</code></li>
            <li><code>α/β + β/α = (α² + β²) / (αβ) = [(α + β)² - 2αβ] / (αβ)</code></li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📦 Cubic Polynomial Relations (Enrichment)</h3>
          <p class="formula">p(x) = ax³ + bx² + cx + d, (a ≠ 0)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>If <em>α, β, γ</em> are zeroes of cubic polynomial <em>p(x)</em>:</li>
            <li><strong>Sum of zeroes:</strong> <code>α + β + γ = -b / a</code></li>
            <li><strong>Sum of products in pairs:</strong> <code>αβ + βγ + γα = c / a</code></li>
            <li><strong>Product of zeroes:</strong> <code>αβγ = -d / a</code></li>
            <li><strong>Cubic form:</strong> <code>k [x³ - (α+β+γ)x² + (αβ+βγ+γα)x - αβγ]</code></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Diagrams Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Visual Concepts: Parabola Shapes &amp; Zeroes of a Quadratic</h2>

      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 1 · Parabola Orientation (a &gt; 0 vs a &lt; 0)</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Parabola orientation depending on coefficient a">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Left: a > 0 (Opens Upwards) -->
              <g transform="translate(10, 10)">
                <text x="100" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0369a1">Case 1: a &gt; 0 (Opens Upward ∪)</text>
                <!-- Axes -->
                <line x1="20" y1="130" x2="190" y2="130" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <line x1="105" y1="35" x2="105" y2="200" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="195" y="134" font-size="10" fill="#64748b">X</text>
                <text x="105" y="30" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Y</text>
                <!-- Curve: 2 intercepts -->
                <path d="M 40 50 Q 105 210 170 50" fill="none" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2.5"/>
                <circle cx="68" cy="130" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
                <circle cx="142" cy="130" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
                <text x="68" y="120" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">α</text>
                <text x="142" y="120" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">β</text>
                <text x="105" y="215" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0369a1" font-weight="600">2 Zeroes (Touches X at 2 points)</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Divider -->
              <line x1="230" y1="20" x2="230" y2="230" stroke="#e2e8f0" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4"/>

              <!-- Right: a < 0 (Opens Downwards) -->
              <g transform="translate(240, 10)">
                <text x="100" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">Case 2: a &lt; 0 (Opens Downward ∩)</text>
                <!-- Axes -->
                <line x1="20" y1="130" x2="190" y2="130" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <line x1="105" y1="35" x2="105" y2="200" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="195" y="134" font-size="10" fill="#64748b">X</text>
                <text x="105" y="30" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Y</text>
                <!-- Curve -->
                <path d="M 40 200 Q 105 40 170 200" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
                <circle cx="68" cy="130" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
                <circle cx="142" cy="130" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
                <text x="68" y="145" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">α</text>
                <text x="142" y="145" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">β</text>
                <text x="105" y="215" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b45309" font-weight="600">Max vertex at top</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">The sign of coefficient <em>a</em> determines whether the parabola opens upwards (a &gt; 0) or downwards (a &lt; 0).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 2 · Number of Real Zeroes (Discriminant D)</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Discriminant cases for number of zeroes">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- 3 Subpanels: D > 0, D = 0, D < 0 -->
              <!-- 1. D > 0: 2 distinct points -->
              <g transform="translate(10, 20)">
                <rect x="5" y="5" width="135" height="190" rx="6" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="72" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">D &gt; 0</text>
                <text x="72" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#047857">Two Distinct Zeroes</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="120" x2="130" y2="120" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M 25 70 Q 72 170 120 70" fill="none" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="2"/>
                <circle cx="43" cy="120" r="3" fill="#dc2626"/>
                <circle cx="102" cy="120" r="3" fill="#dc2626"/>
                <text x="72" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#065f46">2 Intersections</text>
              </g>

              <!-- 2. D = 0: 1 point (tangent) -->
              <g transform="translate(160, 20)">
                <rect x="5" y="5" width="135" height="190" rx="6" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="72" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">D = 0</text>
                <text x="72" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#b45309">Two Equal Zeroes</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="120" x2="130" y2="120" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M 25 60 Q 72 120 120 60" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2"/>
                <circle cx="72" cy="120" r="3.5" fill="#dc2626"/>
                <text x="72" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#92400e">1 Touch Point</text>
              </g>

              <!-- 3. D < 0: 0 points -->
              <g transform="translate(310, 20)">
                <rect x="5" y="5" width="135" height="190" rx="6" fill="#fee2e2" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="72" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#991b1b">D &lt; 0</text>
                <text x="72" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#b91c1c">No Real Zeroes</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="140" x2="130" y2="140" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M 25 70 Q 72 110 120 70" fill="none" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text x="72" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#991b1b">Never touches X</text>
              </g>
              
              <text x="230" y="235" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#64748b" font-weight="500">Discriminant D = b² - 4ac governs the number of real roots.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">A quadratic polynomial intersects the X-axis at 2 points if D &gt; 0, touches at 1 point if D = 0, and does not touch if D &lt; 0.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Solved Step-by-Step Exemplar Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Step-by-Step Solved Problem: Finding Symmetric Expressions</h2>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.75rem; background:var(--paper)">
        <h3 style="color:var(--brand);margin-top:0">Example: If α and β are the zeroes of p(x) = 2x² - 5x + 7, find the value of (1/α + 1/β) and (α² + β²).</h3>
        <div style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text)">
          <p><strong>Step 1 (Extract coefficients):</strong> For <em>2x² - 5x + 7</em>, we have <code>a = 2, b = -5, c = 7</code>.</p>
          <p><strong>Step 2 (Sum and product of zeroes):</strong>
            <br/>• Sum: <code>α + β = -b / a = -(-5) / 2 = 5/2</code>
            <br/>• Product: <code>α · β = c / a = 7/2</code>
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 3 (Calculate 1/α + 1/β):</strong>
            <br/><code>1/α + 1/β = (α + β) / (αβ) = (5/2) / (7/2) = 5/7</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 4 (Calculate α² + β²):</strong>
            <br/>Using identity <code>α² + β² = (α + β)² - 2αβ</code>:
            <br/><code>α² + β² = (5/2)² - 2(7/2) = 25/4 - 7 = 25/4 - 28/4 = -3/4</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Final Answer:</strong> <code>1/α + 1/β = 5/7</code> and <code>α² + β² = -3/4</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Interactive 20-Question Quiz -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Interactive CBSE Board Exam Quiz (20 Questions)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Test your concepts on graphs, zero-coefficient relations, and quadratic formulations with board exam standard MCQs.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container card" id="quiz-box">
        <div class="quiz-header-bar">
          <span class="quiz-counter" id="quiz-counter">Question 1 of 20</span>
          <span class="quiz-score" id="quiz-score">Score: 0 / 20</span>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-question-body">
          <p class="quiz-q-text" id="quiz-question">Loading question...</p>
          <div class="quiz-options-list" id="quiz-options"></div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="quiz-feedback"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-footer-actions">
          <button class="button secondary" id="quiz-prev-btn" disabled>← Previous</button>
          <button class="button" id="quiz-next-btn" disabled>Next Question →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-completed-banner card" id="quiz-result-box" style="display:none; text-align:center; padding:2.5rem;">
        <h3>Quiz Completed! 🎉</h3>
        <p class="quiz-final-score" id="quiz-final-score" style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--brand); margin:1rem 0;"></p>
        <p id="quiz-final-msg" class="muted"></p>
        <button class="button" id="quiz-restart-btn" style="margin-top:1rem;">Retake Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-banner">
      <h2>Need personalized Maths guidance for Class 10?</h2>
      <p>Book a free {provider.trial.duration_minutes}-minute trial session with {provider.tutor_name} (online or at-home) to master algebra, polynomials, and board exam problem solving.</p>
      <a class="button" href={calBookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book Free Trial</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function() {
  const quizData = [
    {
      q: "If one zero of the quadratic polynomial x² + 3x + k is 2, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["10", "-10", "-7", "-2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Since 2 is a zero, p(2) = 0 ⟹ (2)² + 3(2) + k = 0 ⟹ 4 + 6 + k = 0 ⟹ 10 + k = 0 ⟹ k = -10."
    },
    {
      q: "The number of polynomials having zeroes as -2 and 5 is:",
      options: ["1", "2", "3", "More than 3"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "Any polynomial of the form k(x + 2)(x - 5) where k is any non-zero real number has -2 and 5 as zeroes. Since k can take infinitely many values, there are infinitely many (more than 3) polynomials."
    },
    {
      q: "If α and β are the zeroes of the polynomial 2x² - 4x + 5, then the value of α² + β² is:",
      options: ["-1", "1", "-6", "6"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Here a=2, b=-4, c=5. α+β = -(-4)/2 = 2, and αβ = 5/2. α² + β² = (α+β)² - 2αβ = (2)² - 2(5/2) = 4 - 5 = -1."
    },
    {
      q: "The zeroes of the quadratic polynomial x² + 99x + 127 are:",
      options: ["Both positive", "Both negative", "One positive and one negative", "Both equal"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Here a = 1 > 0, b = 99 > 0, c = 127 > 0. Sum of zeroes α+β = -99 (negative) and product αβ = 127 (positive). When the product is positive, both zeroes have the same sign; since their sum is negative, both zeroes must be negative."
    },
    {
      q: "If one zero of the quadratic polynomial (k - 1)x² + kx + 1 is -3, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["4/3", "-4/3", "2/3", "-2/3"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Substitute x = -3: (k - 1)(-3)² + k(-3) + 1 = 0 ⟹ 9(k - 1) - 3k + 1 = 0 ⟹ 9k - 9 - 3k + 1 = 0 ⟹ 6k - 8 = 0 ⟹ k = 8/6 = 4/3."
    },
    {
      q: "A quadratic polynomial whose zeroes are -3 and 4 is:",
      options: ["x² - x + 12", "x² + x + 12", "x²/2 - x/2 - 6", "2x² + 2x - 24"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Sum of zeroes S = -3 + 4 = 1. Product of zeroes P = (-3)(4) = -12. Form: k(x² - Sx + P) = k(x² - x - 12). Taking k = 1/2 gives x²/2 - x/2 - 6."
    },
    {
      q: "The graph of y = p(x) intersects the X-axis at 3 distinct points. The number of zeroes of p(x) is:",
      options: ["0", "1", "2", "3"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "The number of real zeroes of y = p(x) is equal to the number of points where its graph intersects the X-axis. Hence, 3 zeroes."
    },
    {
      q: "If the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial ax² + bx + c (c ≠ 0) are equal, then:",
      options: ["c and a have opposite signs", "c and d have opposite signs", "c and a have the same sign", "b and c have the same sign"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "For equal zeroes, discriminant D = b² - 4ac = 0 ⟹ b² = 4ac. Since b² ≥ 0 for real b, 4ac must be positive, which means ac > 0. Thus, a and c must have the same sign."
    },
    {
      q: "If α, β are zeroes of x² - 6x + k and 3α + 2β = 20, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["-16", "16", "-8", "8"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "α + β = 6 ⟹ 2α + 2β = 12. Given 3α + 2β = 20. Subtracting: α = 20 - 12 = 8. Then β = 6 - α = 6 - 8 = -2. Therefore, k = αβ = 8 × (-2) = -16."
    },
    {
      q: "If one zero of the polynomial p(x) = 5x² + 13x + k is reciprocal of the other, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["0", "5", "1/5", "6"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Let the zeroes be α and 1/α. Product of zeroes = α × (1/α) = 1. In p(x), product of zeroes = c/a = k/5. So k/5 = 1 ⟹ k = 5."
    },
    {
      q: "If the sum of the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial kx² + 2x + 3k is equal to their product, then k equals:",
      options: ["1/3", "-1/3", "2/3", "-2/3"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "Sum of zeroes = -b/a = -2/k. Product of zeroes = c/a = 3k/k = 3. Given Sum = Product ⟹ -2/k = 3 ⟹ k = -2/3."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the degree of a non-zero constant polynomial?",
      options: ["0", "1", "Not defined", "Any real number"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "A constant polynomial such as p(x) = 7 can be written as 7x⁰. Hence its degree is 0. (Note: The zero polynomial p(x) = 0 has undefined degree)."
    },
    {
      q: "If α and β are zeroes of p(x) = x² - p(x + 1) - c = x² - px - (p + c), then (α + 1)(β + 1) is:",
      options: ["c - 1", "1 - c", "c", "1 + c"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "p(x) = x² - px - (p + c). Here α + β = p and αβ = -(p + c). Expanding: (α + 1)(β + 1) = αβ + (α + β) + 1 = -(p + c) + p + 1 = -p - c + p + 1 = 1 - c."
    },
    {
      q: "The zeroes of the quadratic polynomial x² - 3x - m(m + 3) are:",
      options: ["m, m + 3", "-m, m + 3", "m, -(m + 3)", "-m, -(m + 3)"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "x² - 3x - m(m + 3) = x² - (m + 3)x + mx - m(m + 3) = x(x - (m + 3)) + m(x - (m + 3)) = (x + m)(x - (m + 3)). Thus the zeroes are -m and m + 3."
    },
    {
      q: "If α and β are the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial f(x) = x² - 5x + 4, find the value of 1/α + 1/β - 2αβ:",
      options: ["-27/4", "-31/4", "31/4", "27/4"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "α + β = 5 and αβ = 4. 1/α + 1/β - 2αβ = (α + β)/(αβ) - 2αβ = 5/4 - 2(4) = 5/4 - 8 = (5 - 32)/4 = -27/4. Wait, 5/4 - 32/4 = -27/4. Let's verify option A is -27/4."
    },
    {
      q: "Can a quadratic polynomial have more than 2 real zeroes?",
      options: ["Yes, if a = 0", "Yes, if c = 0", "No, at most 2 zeroes", "Yes, if D > 0"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "By the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra, a polynomial of degree n can have at most n real zeroes. For a quadratic polynomial (degree 2), it can have at most 2 zeroes."
    },
    {
      q: "If the zeroes of x² - bx + c are two consecutive integers, then b² - 4c equals:",
      options: ["-1", "0", "1", "2"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Let the zeroes be α and α + 1. Difference between roots is |(α + 1) - α| = 1. We know |α - β| = √(D) / |a| = √(b² - 4c) / 1. Hence √(b² - 4c) = 1 ⟹ b² - 4c = 1."
    },
    {
      q: "If α, β are the zeroes of 2x² + 5x + k such that α² + β² + αβ = 21/4, then k is:",
      options: ["1", "2", "-2", "3"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "α + β = -5/2, αβ = k/2. α² + β² + αβ = (α + β)² - αβ = (-5/2)² - k/2 = 25/4 - k/2. Given 25/4 - k/2 = 21/4 ⟹ k/2 = 25/4 - 21/4 = 4/4 = 1 ⟹ k = 2."
    },
    {
      q: "Which of the following is NOT a polynomial?",
      options: ["√3 x² - 2x + 5", "x² - 3/x + 2", "x³ - 5x + √2", "3x² - 7x + 9"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "In x² - 3/x + 2, the term 3/x = 3x⁻¹ has a negative exponent (-1). A polynomial must have only non-negative integers as exponents of variable x."
    },
    {
      q: "If α and β are zeroes of x² - 4x + 1, then the value of α⁴β³ + α³β⁴ is:",
      options: ["4", "16", "64", "8"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "α⁴β³ + α³β⁴ = α³β³(α + β) = (αβ)³(α + β). In x² - 4x + 1, α + β = 4 and αβ = 1. Thus, (1)³(4) = 1 × 4 = 4."
    }
  ];

  // Fix question 15 answer index to match -27/4: option index 0
  quizData[14].answer = 0;

  let currentIdx = 0;
  let userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);

  const qText = document.getElementById("quiz-question");
  const optionsBox = document.getElementById("quiz-options");
  const feedbackBox = document.getElementById("quiz-feedback");
  const counterBox = document.getElementById("quiz-counter");
  const scoreBox = document.getElementById("quiz-score");
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-prev-btn");
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-next-btn");
  const quizBox = document.getElementById("quiz-box");
  const resultBox = document.getElementById("quiz-result-box");
  const finalScore = document.getElementById("quiz-final-score");
  const finalMsg = document.getElementById("quiz-final-msg");
  const restartBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-restart-btn");

  function renderQuestion(idx) {
    const item = quizData[idx];
    counterBox.textContent = `Question ${idx + 1} of ${quizData.length}`;
    qText.textContent = item.q;
    optionsBox.innerHTML = "";
    feedbackBox.textContent = "";
    feedbackBox.className = "quiz-feedback";

    const selected = userAnswers[idx];

    item.options.forEach((optText, oIdx) => {
      const btn = document.createElement("button");
      btn.className = "quiz-opt-btn";
      btn.textContent = `${String.fromCharCode(65 + oIdx)}. ${optText}`;

      if (selected !== null) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        if (oIdx === item.answer) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-correct");
        } else if (oIdx === selected) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-wrong");
        }
      } else {
        btn.onclick = () => selectOption(oIdx);
      }

      optionsBox.appendChild(btn);
    });

    if (selected !== null) {
      if (selected === item.answer) {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✓ Correct! ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-correct");
      } else {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✗ Incorrect. Correct answer is option ${String.fromCharCode(65 + item.answer)}. ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-wrong");
      }
    }

    prevBtn.disabled = idx === 0;
    nextBtn.disabled = selected === null;
    nextBtn.textContent = idx === quizData.length - 1 ? "Finish Quiz →" : "Next Question →";
    updateScoreDisplay();
  }

  function selectOption(oIdx) {
    userAnswers[currentIdx] = oIdx;
    renderQuestion(currentIdx);
  }

  function updateScoreDisplay() {
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    scoreBox.textContent = `Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length}`;
  }

  prevBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx > 0) {
      currentIdx--;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    }
  };

  nextBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
      currentIdx++;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    } else {
      finishQuiz();
    }
  };

  function finishQuiz() {
    quizBox.style.display = "none";
    resultBox.style.display = "block";
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    finalScore.textContent = `Your Final Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length} (${Math.round((score / quizData.length) * 100)}%)`;
    if (score >= 18) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Mastery level achieved! Excellent command over polynomials and zero-coefficient relationships.";
    } else if (score >= 14) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Good performance! Review algebraic identities and graphical zero interpretations to aim for 100%.";
    } else {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Revise the key formulas above and re-attempt the quiz to strengthen your concepts.";
    }
  }

  restartBtn.onclick = () => {
    userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);
    currentIdx = 0;
    resultBox.style.display = "none";
    quizBox.style.display = "block";
    renderQuestion(0);
  };

  renderQuestion(0);
})();
</script>

